<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leto</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leto was a Greek goddess, daughter of the Titans Coeus and Phoebe and mother by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> of the twin gods <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemis">Artemis</a>. According to myth, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hera">Hera</a>'s jealousy forced her to wander until she gave birth on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delos">Delos</a>. She was worshipped widely, notably at the Letoon in Lycia, and the Cretan city of Lato was named after her.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leto.jpg" alt="Leto" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Phintias · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tityos_Leto_Louvre_G42.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
